 "notes": [
  "Experiment lane kit-vs-hand-valkenburger-20261120 (2026-11-20): the kit route for the 1985-2004 housing-block cluster.",
  "Groups: 0 the NW Valkenburgerstraat front (w02-329L 2021-03-08) as five fronts in a row (dark grey, white bay stack, red, mauve-grey x2); 1 the NW red-brown balcony front (w04-328 2021-03-18); 2 the NE white-render front over a two-storey brown-brick maisonette base with the central loggia (w03-57 2018-05-08); 3 the SE mauve render panels with their two-storey glazed bays (w07-149 2021-12-31); 4 the SE red-brown punched front and stair strips (w06-149 2023-01-13); 5 the SE white render balcony module (w08-153 2024-12-10, washed out).",
  "The SW front (w01-237, 49 m) has no panorama within 35 m and stays in the window grid; the set-back top storey panels stay in the window grid.",
  "Kit route A2 (lane large-kit-gaps-20261121, 2026-11-21): A re-authored with the closed kit gaps: per-house ribbonStoreys and a rendered glazed stack on the Valkenburgerstraat row, glass-block accent panels under the dark front's windows, the Rapenburgerstraat render panel proud of the brick round its glazed columns, the Koerierstersplein loggias lined in brown brick, and residential grounds on Koerierstersplein and Rapenburgerstraat (the Valkenburgerstraat ground keeps its shops: Roche Bobois, BOMBOM). Not installed: hand model B ships."
 ]
}
